w: 1.~A- las! and did my _ Sa- viour bleed, And did my _ Sover- eign die! _ Would he de- vote that sac- red head For such _ a _ worm as I!
w: 2.~Was it for crimes that _ I had done He groaned up- _ on the tree! _ A- ma- zing pi- ty! grace un- known! And love _ be- _ yond de- gree!
w: 3.~Well might the sun in _ dark- ness hide, And shut his _ glo- ries in, _ When Christ, the might- y Ma- ker, died For man _ the _ crea- ture's sin.
w: 4.~Thus might I hide my _ blush- ing face While his dear _ cross ap- pears; _ Dis- solve my heart in thank- ful- ness, And melt _ mine _ eyes in tears.
w: 5.~But drops of grief can _ ne'er re- pay The debt of _ love I owe; _ Here, Lord, I give my- self a- way, 'Tis all _ that _ I can do.
